# Force LF line endings on files that MUST be LF regardless of
# the operator's git core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Background: the Windows operator runs `git config core.autocrlf=true`
# which normalizes all text files to CRLF on checkout. That's fine
# for editors and Markdown but BREAKS bash scripts -- bash chokes on
# `\r` and shell scripts written to disk with CRLF either fail to
# parse, fail to set -u, or hang on a `case` with `\r`-terminated
# patterns. Twice this session (2026-05-29 fuzz + 2026-05-30 soak
# watcher) bash background processes have died silently because git
# rewrote the script after they were already running.
#
# Pattern reference: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes#_text

# Shell scripts: always LF
*.sh           text eol=lf
*.bash         text eol=lf

# WSL-side workflow / systemd assets: always LF
*.service      text eol=lf
*.conf         text eol=lf

# YAML (CI workflows etc): always LF
*.yml          text eol=lf
*.yaml         text eol=lf

# Rust / Cargo: LF is the cargo + crates.io norm
*.rs           text eol=lf
*.toml         text eol=lf

# Docs: LF (most editors handle either, but GitHub renders LF cleaner)
*.md           text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts: CRLF is what Windows expects
*.ps1          text eol=crlf
*.psm1         text eol=crlf
*.psd1         text eol=crlf

# Windows batch files: CRLF
*.bat          text eol=crlf
*.cmd          text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never normalize
*.png          binary
*.jpg          binary
*.jpeg         binary
*.gif          binary
*.ico          binary
*.exe          binary
*.dll          binary
*.so           binary
*.dylib        binary
*.tar.gz       binary
*.zip          binary
*.7z           binary
*.bin          binary
